<title>GREECE: Bank commissions for Greek 2yr zeros at 0.5pct-min.</title>
<headline>Bank commissions for Greek 2yr zeros at 0.5pct-min.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks will get a selling commission of 0.5 percent for the 2-year zero-coupon T-notes to be issued on January 20, Deputy Finance Minister Nickos Chrostodoulakis told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The selling commission for the two-year securities is 0.5 percent,&quot; said Christodoulakis.</p>
<p>The gross yield to maturity for the 2-year zero-coupon T-notes is 10.3 percent. Interest earned on the two-year zeros will be subject to a 7.5 percent tax upon maturity.</p>
<p>It is the first time that Greece issues two-year zero coupons.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
